 pk (p/root pk) [(empty-scope :unit) {}])]\\\\n   224\\\\t    {:unit unit, :scopes scopes}))\\\\n     1\\\\t(ns yang.php.antlr.cst\\\\n     2\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The PHP parser worker (docs/design/yang.php.md section 6): the\\\\n     3\\\\t   grammars-v4 php grammar profile over the generic `yang.antlr.cst` worker.\\\\n     4\\\\t   The generated recognizers come from `bb gen:antlr` (antlr/php/manifest.edn);\\\\n     5\\\\t   the JVM is the only local target. The entry rule is `htmlDocument`.\\\\n     6\\\\t\\\\n     7\\\\t   The grammar's non-standard generics (`typeParameterListInBrackets`, the\\\\n     8\\\\t   `<: ... :>` brackets) are not PHP: a parse that uses them is refused as\\\\n     9\\\\t   `{:yang.php/not-php :generics}` rather than exported.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    10\\\\t  (:require\\\\n    11\\\\t    [yang.antlr.cst :as cst])\\\\n    12\\\\t  (:import\\\\n    13\\\\t    (yang.php.antlr.gen\\\\n    14\\\\t      PhpLexer\\\\n    15\\\\t      PhpParser)))\\\\n    16\\\\t\\\\n    17\\\\t\\\\n    18\\\\t(def grammar-id\\\\n    19\\\\t  \\\\\\\"grammars-v4 php at its pinned revision, generated by ANTLR 4.13.2.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    20\\\\t  \\\\\\\"grammars-v4/php@85e2dd1779ce556111ef98ead5d62a9858e95599 antlr-4.13.2\\\\\\\")\\\\n    21\\\\t\\\\n    22\\\\t\\\\n    23\\\\t(def profile\\\\n    24\\\\t  {:grammar-id grammar-id,\\\\n    25\\\\t   :make-lexer (fn [cs] (PhpLexer. cs)),\\\\n    26\\\\t   :make-parser (fn [ts] (PhpParser. ts)),\\\\n    27\\\\t   :start (fn [^PhpParser p] (.htmlDocument p))})\\\\n    28\\\\t\\\\n    29\\\\t\\\\n    30\\\\t(defn make-worker\\\\n    31\\\\t  []\\\\n    32\\\\t  (cst/make-worker profile))\\\\n    33\\\\t\\\\n    34\\\\t\\\\n    35\\\\t(defn- generics?\\\\n    36\\\\t  [pk]\\\\n    37\\\\t  (boolean (some #(= \\\\\\\"typeParameterListInBrackets\\\\\\\" (:rule %))\\\\n    38\\\\t                 (:yang.cst/nodes pk))))\\\\n    39\\\\t\\\\n    40\\\\t\\\\n    41\\\\t(defn- line-starts\\\\n    42\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The UTF-8 byte offsets at which each source line begins (the line side\\\\n    43\\\\t   table, section 17: derived at the parse boundary, where the source is\\\\n    44\\\\t   known, so no later stage needs the text).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    45\\\\t  [^String source]\\\\n    46\\\\t  (let [bs (.getBytes source \\\\\\\"UTF-8\\\\\\\")]\\\\n    47\\\\t    (into [0] (keep-indexed (fn [i b] (when (= b 10) (inc i)))) bs)))\\\\n    48\\\\t\\\\n    49\\\\t\\\\n    50\\\\t(defn parse-source\\\\n    51\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Parse one complete PHP source string as unit `unit`: the CST packet, or\\\\n    52\\\\t   `{:yang.php/not-php :generics}` when the parse uses the grammar's generics\\\\n    53\\\\t   extension.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    54\\\\t  ([source] (parse-source (make-worker) [:unit 0] source))\\\\n    55\\\\t  ([worker unit source]\\\\n    56\\\\t   (let [pk (cst/parse-unit worker unit source)]\\\\n    57\\\\t     (if (generics? pk)\\\\n    58\\\\t       {:yang.php/not-php :generics}\\\\n    59\\\\t       (assoc pk :yang.php/line-starts (line-starts source))))))\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_13\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The existing dynamic-scope model gives eval a useful starting point: functions with eval are marked for a heap scope, and included units already accept the caller’s `%scope` and `%ctx`. I’m checking how to reuse that path without reinitializing PHP state or resetting the run’s safepoint counter.\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_14\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1,160p;230,380p;1740,1885p;3075,3140p;3180,3235p;3610,3807p;3835,3860p;3990,4048p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_14\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1,160p;230,380p;1740,1885p;3075,3140p;3180,3235p;3610,3807p;3835,3860p;3990,4048p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t(ns yang.php.antlr.lower\\\\n     2\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The PHP lowering interpreter: CST packets in, Universal AST program\\\\n     3\\\\t   batches out (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 3, 7). Portable.\\\\n     4\\\\t\\\\n     5\\\\t   Per packet: validate the tree, analyze scopes (`yang.php.antlr.scope`),\\\\n     6\\\\t   then lower with one `case` arm per grammar rule. A rule P1 does not lower\\\\n     7\\\\t   fails with `:yang.php/unsupported` naming the rule and construct; a rule\\\\n     8\\\\t   with no arm fails with `:yang.php/unhandled-rule`. Nothing is silently\\\\n     9\\\\t   dropped.\\\\n    10\\\\t\\\\n    11\\\\t   Decided lowering rules (collab/1792905000000 plan):\\\\n    12\\\\t   - A top-level `$x` is `(php/global-get \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")` / `(php/global-set! \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" v)`;\\\\n    13\\\\t     inside a function it is a lexical cell `$x` allocated at entry holding\\\\n    14\\\\t     `:php/undef`. Loops are self-applied `:loop`-marked lambdas whose\\\\n    15\\\\t     `break`/`continue` are `php/call-ec` escapes bound to `%brk<id>` and\\\\n    16\\\\t     `%cont<id>`, created only when the body uses them; the `:loops` stack of\\\\n    17\\\\t     the context resolves `break n`. `switch` is one stack level: a chain of\\\\n    18\\\\t     lambdas whose bodies tail-call the next case.\\\\n    19\\\\t   - A function is `(php/declare-function! name (php/make-function name spec\\\\n    20\\\\t     (fn [%fn %args] body) statics))`; top-level unconditional declarations\\\\n    21\\\\t     are hoisted. `return` is an escape from `php/call-ec`, bound only when\\\\n    22\\\\t     the body has a `return`.\\\\n    23\\\\t   - The unit is its hoisted top-level function declarations, then its\\\\n    24\\\\t     statements in order, run under `php/run-main`.\\\\n    25\\\\t   - Inline HTML is `(php/echo \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"bytes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")`; `echo a, b` is\\\\n    26\\\\t     `(php/echo (php/to-string a))` per operand; a PHP string is a byte\\\\n    27\\\\t     carrier (a latin-1 string), literal text resolved here to UTF-8 bytes.\\\\n    28\\\\t   - `&&`, `||`, `and`, `or`, `?:` are `:if` nodes over `php/to-bool`, never\\\\n    29\\\\t     applications, so they short circuit. Every other operator is one\\\\n    30\\\\t     application of a `php/` function of the prelude.\\\\n    31\\\\t   - A call `f(a, b)` resolves `f` before any argument runs:\\\\n    32\\\\t     `(let [%f (php/resolve-fn \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"f\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"F\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")] (php/call %f [a b]))`.\\\\n    33\\\\t   - Generated names are `%<prefix><cst-id>`; `%` cannot begin a PHP name, so\\\\n    34\\\\t     no guest name shadows a name the lowering emits. The lowering never\\\\n    35\\\\t     names a runtime key (`php.rt/*`).\\\\n    36\\\\t\\\\n    37\\\\t   Diagnostic namespace: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"yang.php\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\"\\\\n    38\\\\t  (:require\\\\n    39\\\\t    [clojure.string :as str]\\\\n    40\\\\t    [clojure.walk :as walk]\\\\n    41\\\\t    [dao.host.text :as text]\\\\n    42\\\\t    [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\\\n    43\\\\t    [yang.antlr.packet :as p]\\\\n    44\\\\t    [yang.core.lower :as core]\\\\n    45\\\\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\\\\n    46\\\\t    [yang.core.stage :as core-stage]\\\\n    47\\\\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\\\\n    48\\\\t    [yang.php.antlr.builtins :as builtins]\\\\n    49\\\\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\\\\n    50\\\\t    [yang.php.antlr.scope :as scope]\\\\n    51\\\\t    [yang.stage :as stage]\\\\n    52\\\\t    [yin.vm :as vm]\\\\n    53\\\\t    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\\\\n    54\\\\t\\\\n    55\\\\t\\\\n    56\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n    57\\\\t;; Diagnostics\\\\n    58\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n    59\\\\t\\\\n    60\\\\t(def ^:private diagnostic-ns \\\\\\\"yang.php\\\\\\\")\\\\n    61\\\\t\\\\n    62\\\\t\\\\n    63\\\\t(defn- unsupported!\\\\n    64\\\\t  [n construct]\\\\n    65\\\\t  (core/unsupported! diagnostic-ns \\\\\\\"PHP\\\\\\\" n construct))\\\\n    66\\\\t\\\\n    67\\\\t\\\\n    68\\\\t(defn- compile-error!\\\\n    69\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A PHP compile-time error: the program is refused, never run.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    70\\\\t  [n message]\\\\n    71\\\\t  (throw (ex-info message\\\\n    72\\\\t                  {:yang.php/diagnostic :yang.php/compile-error,\\\\n    73\\\\t                   :rule (:rule n),\\\\n    74\\\\t                   :span (:span n)})))\\\\n    75\\\\t\\\\n    76\\\\t\\\\n    77\\\\t(defn- warn!\\\\n    78\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Record a warning-severity lowering diagnostic: the program still lowers.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    79\\\\t  [ctx n kind message data]\\\\n    80\\\\t  (swap! (:warnings ctx)\\\\n    81\\\\t         conj\\\\n    82\\\\t         (merge {:yang.php/diagnostic kind,\\\\n    83\\\\t                 :severity :warning,\\\\n    84\\\\t                 :message message,\\\\n    85\\\\t                 :span (:span n)}\\\\n    86\\\\t                data)))\\\\n    87\\\\t\\\\n    88\\\\t\\\\n    89\\\\t(def unsupported-rules\\\\n    90\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Grammar rules P1 does not lower, with the construct each names.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    91\\\\t  {\\\\\\\"gotoStatement\\\\\\\" :goto,\\\\n    92\\\\t   \\\\\\\"declareStatement\\\\\\\" :declare,\\\\n    93\\\\t   \\\\\\\"importStatement\\\\\\\" :import,\\\\n    94\\\\t   \\\\\\\"newExpr\\\\\\\" :new,\\\\n    95\\\\t   \\\\\\\"yieldExpression\\\\\\\" :yield,\\\\n    96\\\\t   \\\\\\\"scriptText\\\\\\\" :inline-script,\\\\n    97\\\\t   \\\\\\\"classConstant\\\\\\\" :class-constant})\\\\n    98\\\\t\\\\n    99\\\\t\\\\n   100\\\\t(def ^:private prefix-refusals\\\\n   101\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Expression forms led by a keyword or operator token.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   102\\\\t  {\\\\\\\"Clone\\\\\\\" :clone,\\\\n   103\\\\t   \\\\\\\"New\\\\\\\" :new,\\\\n   104\\\\t   \\\\\\\"Eval\\\\\\\" :eval,\\\\n   105\\\\t   \\\\\\\"Include\\\\\\\" :include,\\\\n   106\\\\t   \\\\\\\"IncludeOnce\\\\\\\" :include,\\\\n   107\\\\t   \\\\\\\"Require\\\\\\\" :include,\\\\n   108\\\\t   \\\\\\\"RequireOnce\\\\\\\" :include,\\\\n   109\\\\t   \\\\\\\"Yield\\\\\\\" :yield,\\\\n   110\\\\t   \\\\\\\"List\\\\\\\" :list})\\\\n   111\\\\t\\\\n   112\\\\t\\\\n   113\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   114\\\\t;; Unit paths and linker names (plan P6 R2/R3)\\\\n   115\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   116\\\\t\\\\n   117\\\\t(def ^:private unit-path-chars #\\\\\\\"[A-Za-z0-9_\\\\\\\\-./]*\\\\\\\")\\\\n   118\\\\t\\\\n   119\\\\t\\\\n   120\\\\t(defn normalize-unit-path\\\\n   121\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`{:path p}` for the relative path `s` normalized (segments joined by `/`,\\\\n   122\\\\t   `.` and empty segments dropped, `..` collapsed), else `{:error e}`:\\\\n   123\\\\t   `:unit-path` for a character outside `[A-Za-z0-9_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\-./]`, `:include-path`\\\\n   124\\\\t   for an absolute path or one escaping the composition root.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   125\\\\t  [s]\\\\n   126\\\\t  (cond\\\\n   127\\\\t    (not (re-matches unit-path-chars s)) {:error :unit-path}\\\\n   128\\\\t    (str/starts-with? s \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\") {:error :include-path}\\\\n   129\\\\t    :else (let [segs (reduce (fn [acc seg]\\\\n   130\\\\t                               (cond\\\\n   131\\\\t                                 (or (= seg \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\") (= seg \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\")) acc\\\\n   132\\\\t                                 (= seg \\\\\\\"..\\\\\\\") (if (empty? acc) (reduced nil) (pop acc))\\\\n   133\\\\t                                 :else (conj acc seg)))\\\\n   134\\\\t                             []\\\\n   135\\\\t                             (str/split s #\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"))]\\\\n   136\\\\t            (if (or (nil? segs) (empty? segs))\\\\n   137\\\\t              {:error :include-path}\\\\n   138\\\\t              {:path (str/join \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\" segs)}))))\\\\n   139\\\\t\\\\n   140\\\\t\\\\n   141\\\\t(defn path-module-symbol\\\\n   142\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The linker module of unit path `path`: `phpm.` then the path with `/` as\\\\n   143\\\\t   `$` and `.` as `$$`, nothing dropped (injective: plan P6 R2).\\\\\\\"\\\\n   144\\\\t  [path]\\\\n   145\\\\t  (symbol (str \\\\\\\"phpm.\\\\\\\" (str/replace (str/replace path \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$\\\\\\\") \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"$$\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n   146\\\\t\\\\n   147\\\\t\\\\n   148\\\\t(def classmap-name\\\\n   149\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The unit name of the autoload class map; a unit path cannot begin with\\\\n   150\\\\t   `$`, so no unit collides with it.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   151\\\\t  \\\\\\\"$classmap\\\\\\\")\\\\n   152\\\\t\\\\n   153\\\\t\\\\n   154\\\\t(def classmap-module\\\\n   155\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The linker module of the class map.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   156\\\\t  (path-module-symbol classmap-name))\\\\n   157\\\\t\\\\n   158\\\\t\\\\n   159\\\\t(defn- path-dirname\\\\n   160\\\\t  \\\\\\\"PHP's `dirname` of the relative path `p`: `.` for a root unit.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   230\\\\t      (if (>= i len)\\\\n   231\\\\t        out\\\\n   232\\\\t        (let [c (subs body i (inc i))\\\\n   233\\\\t              e (when (< (inc i) len) (subs body (inc i) (+ i 2)))]\\\\n   234\\\\t          (cond\\\\n   235\\\\t            (not (and (= c \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") e))\\\\n   236\\\\t            (let [cp (first (text/code-points (subs body i (min len (+ i 2)))))]\\\\n   237\\\\t              (recur (+ i (if (> cp 0xFFFF) 2 1)) (into out (utf8-of-code-point cp))))\\\\n   238\\\\t            (contains? simple-escapes e)\\\\n   239\\\\t            (recur (+ i 2) (conj out (get simple-escapes e)))\\\\n   240\\\\t            (re-matches #\\\\\\\"[0-7]\\\\\\\" e)\\\\n   241\\\\t            (let [digits (re-find #\\\\\\\"^[0-7]{1,3}\\\\\\\" (subs body (inc i)))]\\\\n   242\\\\t              (recur (+ i 1 (count digits))\\\\n   243\\\\t                     (conj out (bit-and (octal-value digits) 255))))\\\\n   244\\\\t            (and (= e \\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\") (re-find #\\\\\\\"^[0-9a-fA-F]{1,2}\\\\\\\" (subs body (+ i 2))))\\\\n   245\\\\t            (let [digits (re-find #\\\\\\\"^[0-9a-fA-F]{1,2}\\\\\\\" (subs body (+ i 2)))]\\\\n   246\\\\t              (recur (+ i 2 (count digits)) (conj out (hex-value digits))))\\\\n   247\\\\t            (and (= e \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\") (re-find #\\\\\\\"^\\\\\\\\{([0-9a-fA-F]+)\\\\\\\\}\\\\\\\" (subs body (+ i 2))))\\\\n   248\\\\t            (let [[whole digits] (re-find #\\\\\\\"^\\\\\\\\{([0-9a-fA-F]+)\\\\\\\\}\\\\\\\" (subs body (+ i 2)))]\\\\n   249\\\\t              (recur (+ i 2 (count whole)) (into out (utf8-of-code-point (hex-value digits)))))\\\\n   250\\\\t            :else (recur (inc i) (conj out 92))))))))\\\\n   251\\\\t\\\\n   252\\\\t\\\\n   253\\\\t(defn- unescape-single\\\\n   254\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The text of the single-quoted string body `body`: only `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\` and `\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'`\\\\n   255\\\\t   are escapes, resolved in one left-to-right scan.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   256\\\\t  [body]\\\\n   257\\\\t  (let [len (count body)]\\\\n   258\\\\t    (loop [i 0\\\\n   259\\\\t           out (transient [])]\\\\n   260\\\\t      (if (>= i len)\\\\n   261\\\\t        (apply str (persistent! out))\\\\n   262\\\\t        (let [c (subs body i (inc i))\\\\n   263\\\\t              e (when (< (inc i) len) (subs body (inc i) (+ i 2)))]\\\\n   264\\\\t          (if (and (= c \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") (contains? #{\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\"} e))\\\\n   265\\\\t            (recur (+ i 2) (conj! out e))\\\\n   266\\\\t            (recur (in