\\\\t   without them: each is handed out exactly once.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  1205\\\\t  [state]\\\\n  2230\\\\t  #{:dao.stream.waitset/unsupported-reason\\\\n  2231\\\\t    :dao.stream.waitset/unresolved\\\\n  2232\\\\t    :dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer})\\\\n  2233\\\\t\\\\n  2234\\\\t\\\\n  2235\\\\t(defn- terminal-resume-outcome\\\\n  2236\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The outcome a woken entry resolved with, when it is one the immediate\\\\n  2237\\\\t   path raises as an error. `handle-put` and `handle-next` raise exactly\\\\n  2238\\\\t   the declared error outcomes of their operation, and whether the first\\\\n  2239\\\\t   attempt blocked must not change that. An outcome outside this contract\\\\n  2240\\\\t   version is the shaped refusal on the immediate path, so it is the\\\\n  2241\\\\t   shaped refusal here too, never a raise. A waitset diagnostic is\\\\n  2242\\\\t   terminal whatever the entry's `:reason` -- an unsupported reason is by\\\\n  2243\\\\t   definition outside the `#{:next :put}` this check otherwise reads --\\\\n  2244\\\\t   so it is named here rather than falling through to the restore. An\\\\n  2245\\\\t   entry that was never polled carries no status.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  2246\\\\t  [entry]\\\\n  2247\\\\t  (let [status (:status entry)]\\\\n  2248\\\\t    (cond\\\\n  2249\\\\t      (contains? waitset-diagnostics status) status\\\\n  2250\\\\t      (= :link-refused status) status\\\\n  2251\\\\t      (contains? ffi/response-loss-statuses status) status\\\\n  2252\\\\t      (contains? #{:next :put} (:reason entry))\\\\n  2253\\\\t      (when (contains? (get wake-error-outcomes (:reason entry)) status)\\\\n  2254\\\\t        status))))\\\\n  2255\\\\t\\\\n  2256\\\\t\\\\n  2257\\\\t(defn- throw-terminal-resume!\\\\n  2258\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Fail a resumed entry exactly as the immediate operation would have. A\\\\n  2259\\\\t   waitset diagnostic names its status and the entry that earned it: there\\\\n  2260\\\\t   is no stream operation whose error vocabulary it belon