g PHP parity. The registry, lexical site selection, directive handling, dispatch, generator behavior, and linked site-set publication/derivation have not been implemented.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFixture chronology: the predecessor recorded sequence, loop-body, function-call and generator-resume red with empty output, and the include case timed out. No fixture was turned green in this session. All fixtures retain \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'`:oracle :pending`; Docker was not run. The linked include handoff remains unimplemented; no new include run was attempted. The predecessor'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'s exact isolated command \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'`timeout 90 clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.ticks-test -v yang.php.antlr.ticks-test/include-handoff-test` timed out after 90 seconds; its combined run timed out after 120 seconds.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSequential gates in this session:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| Gate | Result | Duration |\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.safepoint-test` | pass, 9 tests / 20 assertions | 3.802 s |\\\\\\\\n| `cljstyle check src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc` | pass | 0.2 s |\\\\\\\\n| `clojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc` | 0 errors, 0 warnings | 6.5 s |\\\\\\\\n| PHP tick, lowering, prelude and e2e; Python trace gates | not run in this session | — |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe requested implementation and acceptance gates remain outstanding. Earlier green and timeout results are recorded in part B'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'s findings; they are not new results from this session.\\\\\\\\nEOF\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:45:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_23\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"git add src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md && git commit -m 'feat(php): declare statement ticks profile' && git push\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:46:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_23\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"git add src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md && git commit -m 'feat(php): declare statement ticks profile' && git push\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Running formatters on staged files...\\\\\\\\nFormatting complete.\\\\\\\\n[p7b-ticks 38375bf7] feat(php): declare statement ticks profile\\\\\\\\n 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+)\\\\\\\\n create mode 100644 collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md\\\\\\\\nTo github.com:sonwh98/datomworld.git\\\\\\\\n   411c2b08..38375bf7  p7b-ticks -> p7b-ticks\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log:47:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_24\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"agent_message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"**The PHP ticks integration is incomplete.** I added the independent `:after` ticks profile and pushed it in commit `38375bf7`, but it is not wired into execution. The staged fixtures remain red; the registry, statement-site lowering, firing rule, generator behavior, and linked include handoff are still outstanding.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe shared safepoint test passed (9 tests, 20 assertions), and the touched source file passed cljstyle and kondo. I did not run the PHP or Python gates in this session.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe task specifies a counter per `declare` site, while the cited slice-3 design describes a request-wide counter. The explicit task instruction takes precedence for implementation; I recorded the discrepancy for parity review.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDetails and the predecessor’s include timeout command are in the [part C findings](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p7b/collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md).\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n---\\\\ndescription: Lead System Architect role definition for datom.world\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# ROLE: Lead System Architect\\\\n\\\\n## Domain Scope\\\\n\\\\n- Foundational axioms, architectural invariants, and design contracts\\\\n- Subsystem boundaries, interpreters, host isolation, and explicit causality\\\\n- Cross-platform architecture, migration strategy, and compatibility boundaries\\\\n- ADR coherence, domain vocabulary, and theoretical grounding where useful\\\\n- Architecture review for high-risk or cross-cutting changes\\\\n- Commit sign-off: the sign-off on completed, review-reconciled work that\\\\n  authorizes the orchestrator to stage, commit, merge, and push it\\\\n  (trivial direct edits are exempt; see\\\\n  [`orchestrator.md`](orchestrator.md#coordination-contract))\\\\n\\\\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\\\\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\\\\n\\\\n## Core Responsibilities\\\\n\\\\n1. **Protect Invariants**: Strictly enforce the 6 non-negotiable invariants (no hidden global state, no implicit control flow, no raw callbacks, no shared mutable state, no layer collapsing, no assumed graphs).\\\\n2. **Decompose Complexity**: When new requirements emerge, decompose them into append-only streams, explicit interpreters, and immutable datom representations.\\\\n3. **Malleability Governance**: Ensure architecture adheres to bounded complexity, loose coupling, and high cohesion as defined in [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../malleability.md).\\\\n4. **Lineage Alignment**: Keep designs grounded in Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp architectural lineage.\\\\n\\\\n## Delegation Prompt Template\\\\n\\\\n```text\\\\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\\\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\\\n\\\\n# Task: <Task Name>\\\\n\\\\nRole: Lead System Architect\\\\n\\\\nImplementers:\\\\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\\\\n\\\\nPerform a read-only architecture review of <design-change>.\\\\n\\\\nRead first:\\\\n- docs/design/datom.world.md\\\\n- <target-design-file>\\\\n- <relevant-implementation-boundary>\\\\n- <relevant-contract-tests>\\\\n\\\\nEvaluate foundational invariants, ownership boundaries, explicit state and\\\\ncontrol flow, concurrency and linearization, dynamic extension, host isolation,\\\\nCLJ/CLJS/CLJD portability, migration risk, completion criteria, and design\\\\ncontradictions. Distinguish architectural defects from implementation gaps or\\\\nintentionally deferred work. Do not edit files.\\\\n\\\\nBegin the final response exactly with:\\\\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\\\\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\\\\n\\\\nThen report: severity | file:line | invariant/evidence | recommended correction.\\\\nAlso confirm the requested properties that passed review.\\\\n```\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-php/1794567570000-architect-ticks-counter-ruling.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:53:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_27\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 - <<'P7B_WRITE_FINDINGS'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\ncontent = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-13 11:04:20 GMT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-13 18:04:20 +0700\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRole: Architect, slice-3 design consult\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nReviewed checkout: p7b-ticks @ 38375bf7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nStatus: counter ruling complete; implementation and formal corpus acceptance remain outstanding\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Ruling: one counter per PHP request, with the threshold supplied by each selected statement-completion hook.** There is no counter per declare occurrence, source file, function/op_array, closure, or generator. Lexical scope controls which completion sites exist and their thresholds; it does not partition the runtime count.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis is supported both by PHP-8.3 source inspection and direct execution of 21 small programs on shiva's PHP 8.3.35 oracle image. All five staged expectations match. This consult changes only this findings artifact: no source, test, design-document, fixture-provenance, or branch changes; no commit or push.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Findings and reconciliation**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Severity | Location | Evidence / required correction |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| P1 — contradictory implementation instruction | \\\\\\\"'`collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.prompt.md:20` | The explicit “a count is per declare-site, PHP semantics” instruction is incorrect. Replace it with the request-owned counter rule in this ruling. Part C was right to escalate the conflict instead of claiming parity. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Resolved — slice-3 ownership | \\\\\\\"'`collab/orch-lane/1794700000000-architect-safepoint-slice3-design.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:103` | The text explicitly says “request-owned counter” and says state survives calls, includes, and generator switches. Its lifecycle table at lines 123–127 and implementation assignment at line 257 reinforce that contract. The implementer'\\\\\\\"'s request-wide reading is correct. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| P2 — stale design status/timing | \\\\\\\"'`docs/design/yang.php.md:1938` | §12 still says sites are before statements and the generic extension refuses non-lambdas. The implemented after-wrapper is at `src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:153`; PHP'\\\\\\\"'s profile is at \\\\\\\"'`src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc:13`. Reconcile §12 in the implementation round. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| P1 — acceptance does not discriminate ownership | \\\\\\\"'`test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p7b.cljc:10` | Every staged tick threshold is 1. All these outputs can pass with an incorrectly partitioned counter. Add N>1 boundary/threshold cases below before claiming counter parity. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| P2 — oracle exit status is insufficient for pending rows | \\\\\\\"'`src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:558` | Pending rows are excluded from failures, while `check-p7-fixture` at line 492 deliberately leaves their `:pass?` false. Read and compare actual records; exit 0 / “failures: 0” alone proves no parity for these rows. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI own the reconciliation failure between the design, stale documentation, and implementation brief. The slice-3 counter paragraph itself was explicit, not ambiguous. Its omission of a compact lexical-versus-runtime decision table made the broader artifact set easier to misread. At this checkout, neither §12 nor the §15 P7-b row (\\\\\\\"'`yang.php.md:2106`) actually specifies a per-declare counter; §15 requires PHP-equivalent tick counts. File-scoped compilation does not imply file-owned execution state.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**PHP 8.3 source evidence**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe links below refer to the PHP-8.3 branch inspected for this consult; line numbers are ordinary one-based file lines. They are source references, not a claim that the moving branch is the exact source hash of the oracle image.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Zend/zend_globals.h:187](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_globals.h#L187): \\\\\\\"'`ticks_count` is a field of executor globals.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Zend/zend_execute_API.c:151](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_execute_API.c#L151): \\\\\\\"'`init_executor()` initializes it to zero for execution/request startup.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Zend/zend_execute.c:5153](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_execute.c#L5153) includes generated \\\\\\\"'`zend_vm_execute.h`. The tick handler'\\\\\\\"'s maintained definition is [Zend/zend_vm_def.h:7439–7452](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_vm_def.h#L7439). Its test is \\\\\\\"'`(uint32_t)++EG(ticks_count) >= opline->extended_value`; it resets the count before calling the tick dispatcher. It counts even when no dispatcher is installed. This is an executor-global accumulator and an instruction-local threshold, not op_array-local state.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Compiler mechanism: [Zend/zend_compile.c:344–361](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L344) initializes a new file's compile-time ticks setting to zero and restores the prior file context on exit. [Lines 5938–5994](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L5938) convert the directive literal to a long, update that setting, compile a block, and restore its prior setting; the semicolon form leaves it changed. [Lines 7065–7200](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L7065) switch function op_arrays without starting a fresh file context. [Lines 9784–9785](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L9784) emit ticks after selected statements when the setting is nonzero. [Lines 2110–2121](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L2110) place that setting in the instruction's extended operand and suppress adjacent duplicate tick emission. [Lines 2518–2522](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L2518) enumerate excluded statement categories; [lines 9659–9668](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L9659) separately handle top-level function/class declarations. A blanket “hook every AST statement” translation is insufficient.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Zend/zend_vm_def.h:7867–7874](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_vm_def.h#L7867): yield saves the next instruction and returns. [Zend/zend_generators.c:706–828](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_generators.c#L706) restores execution frames/JIT context around resume, not a saved tick count.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ext/standard/basic_functions.c:1549–1569](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/basic_functions.c#L1549): user tick dispatch guards each executing registered entry against reentry. Do not replace this with a global “ticks busy” rule that stops counting all guest tick sites. Registered callback arguments are its registration arguments, not the line/unit/threshold operands.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThus switching files or op_arrays changes the instructions being executed, and possibly their embedded thresholds, without selecting a different counter. The runtime probes below independently confirm the relevant observable consequences.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Normative decision table for the implementer**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Concern | Required behavior |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|---|---|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Counter owner | Allocate one explicit guest request-owned counter, initially 0, shared by all PHP tick hooks in that request. Keep it in existing guest execution/store machinery; introduce no host global or shared process state. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Increment and firing | On each selected normal completion, increment once. If the new count is **greater than or equal to** that site's N, reset to 0 **before** dispatching registered handlers. Do not use equality, modulo, subtraction of N, or a threshold-global “current N.” |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Reset points | Request initialization and threshold firing only. No reset at declare entry/exit, function call/return, include/return, registration/unregistration, generator switch, or exception/context restoration. A new independent request starts from zero. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Empty registry | Continue incrementing/resetting at selected sites. Registration changes dispatch membership, not counter phase. Confirmed by the empty-registry probe. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Lexical N | Each mark carries its own effective compile-time N. An inner block directive overrides the enclosing value for its body; exiting that block restores the outer value for subsequent emitted sites. Entering/leaving either block does not reset the accumulated count. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| N=0 | That lexical region contributes no tick instructions for its own statements; it does not clear accumulated progress. An enclosing nonzero context may still select the completion of the declare construct itself. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Directive syntax | Preserve block versus semicolon behavior and Zend's statement-selection/adjacent-suppression behavior. A directive can itself lead to a tick: the measured semicolon case below produces ATB, not ABT. There is no extra generic “enter declare” runtime reset or hook. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| N validation/range | Ordinary positive integer thresholds and zero are the cases established here. Do not invent “all N<=0 disable ticks”: Zend's literal conversion and unsigned instruction operand are separate concerns. Broader literal/range acceptance needs its own oracle cases or an explicit supported-subset refusal. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Functions and closures | Retain body-site thresholds from compilation. A call from ticked code does not dynamically instrument an unticked body. A ticked body contributes to the same request count even when called from unticked code or after its defining include has returned. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Generator yield/resume | Preserve the pending after-hook in the continuation. Suspension itself does not complete the yield statement. On eventual normal completion run that hook once using the then-current request counter. Repeated inspection of a suspended value does not replay it. Never snapshot/restore the count with generator context. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Nonlocal exit | A statement whose normal completion is bypassed contributes no after-hook. Already completed sites retain their count effects through throw/unwind. A callback exception cannot undo the reset that preceded dispatch. A pending hook is not a finally hook. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Include/include_once | Included code has its own lexical sites/N; the caller's pragma is not inherited dynamically. All executed sites share the request counter. Repeated includes revisit their sites; a skipped once body contributes none. A selected caller include statement still completes and can tick even when the once body is skipped. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Budget/profile separation | Statement ticks do not charge \\\\\\\"'`php.sp/tick`, the existing execution-budget hook. Preserve independently selected `:call`/`:loop` sites and the shared VM semantics. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe intended profile and operand contract remains exactly:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```clojure'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{:line {:hook 'php.sp/line :operands true :after true}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n[:line n {:unit unit-path :ticks N}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; derives:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(php.sp/line n {:unit unit-path :ticks N})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nHere \\\\\\\"'`n` and `:unit` identify the source occurrence; neither is a counter key. `:ticks` is the effective instruction threshold, not a declaration identifier. The generic safepoint stage transports literals and performs value-preserving normal-completion placement; PHP lowering owns eligible-site selection and PHP runtime code owns counting/dispatch. Omitting `:line` from a derivation profile omits these hooks; canonical program rows remain unchanged.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Include-site handoff remains a landing requirement**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source-unit operand does not itself transport marks through publication. At \\\\\\\"'`src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc:42`, `:site-set` is still nil. Preserve slice-3 lines 133–154: publish and retrieve verified occurrence site sets bound to the canonical root/source association; derive included executable images using the selected ticks profile; pin the hook dependency and derived images; handle SCC bundles and repin member aliases. Missing required metadata must fail closed, whereas a verified empty set for an unticked unit is legitimate.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEvery derived module must resolve the same request's hook/state. Including a module must not reinitialize the tick registry or accumulator. A retained closure keeps its defining unit's operands and uses the active request's shared counter. No extra counter indexed by declaration, unit, or line is needed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Measured fixture evidence**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nExecuted on \\\\\\\"'`shiva.stigmergy.systems`, 2026-11-13, in fresh disposable containers per program. Existing tag `php:8.3-cli` reports PHP 8.3.35 CLI NTS / Zend 4.3.35, built 2026-10-06. The shorter `php:8.3` tag was not installed; no image was pulled.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Image ID: \\\\\\\"'`sha256:7855de8f54c32ffc92720b20b550f2dbc1c82c2000c7a850ccf350f71c36293f`'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Repository digest: \\\\\\\"'`php@sha256:aafe21201943a8a6e497ddfb471e2ce68ada76adede38c7d61fede8918b24319`'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEach main program and included unit was placed in a temporary directory, mounted read-only at /w, with this invocation:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```sh'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndocker run --rm --pull=never --network=none --read-only \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -v <temporary-directory>:/w:ro -w /w php:8.3-cli php \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -d display_errors=1 -d html_errors=0 -d error_reporting=E_ALL \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -d log_errors=0 -d auto_prepend_file=/w/pre.php main.php\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe unticked pre.php was the exact staged prologue:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<?php function tick_handler() { echo 'T'; } register_tick_function('tick_handler');\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis matches the P7 oracle runner's prepend-unit arrangement. Every one of the 21 executions exited 0 with empty stderr and exactly the stdout recorded here, with no diagnostics. Temporary directories were removed. These are independent direct PHP oracle measurements, **not** a run of the Clojure \\\\\\\"'`--p7` wrapper or of yang.php.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Fixture and source location | Staged expected | Measured PHP 8.3.35 | Interpretation |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|---|---|---|---|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| sequence, \\\\\\\"'`programs_p7b.cljc:10` | ATTBT | ATTBT | Three completions: echo A, assignment, echo B. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| loop-body, line 12 | ATAT | ATAT | Only the inner declared body is ticked; loop machinery is outside its directive. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| function-call, line 14 | FT | FT | f's body is unticked; the call statement's normal completion ticks. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| generator-resume, line 16 | ATBT | ATBT | current() suspends at yield; A prints; next() completes yield and ticks, then B completes and ticks. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| include-handoff, line 19 | LT | LT | Included lib.php owns a ticked echo site; the caller is unticked. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe sequence variants also confirm the slice-3 proposals: N=2 gives ATB; N=0 gives AB.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Oracle acceptance ruling**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThere is no remaining choice between counter architectures: the source mechanism and the N>1 measurements settle it in favor of the request-owned count. PHP remains the authority for exact site selection and observable output if a lowering prediction disagrees.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe formal \\\\\\\"'`--p7` pass on shiva MUST compare all five current IDs: `:sequence`, `:loop-body`, `:function-call`, `:generator-resume`, and `:include-handoff`, including output, absence of diagnostics/uncaught errors, and successful exit. Record actual version, image digest, host, and date. Do not infer a passing fixture from the current runner'\\\\\\\"'s pending-row exit status. This consult leaves all \\\\\\\"'`:oracle :pending` fields untouched.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor counter-ownership acceptance, the implementer must add and oracle-confirm at least separate-declares, nested-threshold, cross-function, cross-include, and generator-shared from the appendix. Also retain the zero-gap, unticked-include, registration/empty-registry, retained-closure, exception, once-skip, and semicolon regressions. The original five N=1 rows cannot replace these discriminators. P7-b's remaining lowering/runtime/linking gates and the broader slice-3 callback/escape/cleanup cases remain required; this consult is not implementation sign-off.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Reproducible additional probes**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEach source below is main.php after an opening PHP tag, with the same separate pre.php above. Where shown, lib.php is a separate file. Outputs are observations, not new hand-derived goldens.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**sequence-n2 — measured \\\\\\\"'`ATB`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; \\\\\\\"'$x = 1; echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**sequence-n0 — measured \\\\\\\"'`AB`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=0) { echo 'A'; \\\\\\\"'$x = 1; echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**separate-declares — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; } declare(ticks=2) { echo 'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**nested-threshold — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABCTD`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=5) { echo 'A'; \\\\\\\"'$x=1; echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; declare(ticks=2) { echo 'C'; } echo 'D'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**zero-gap — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABCT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=3) { echo 'A'; } declare(ticks=0) { echo 'B'; } declare(ticks=3) { echo 'C'; \\\\\\\"'$x=1; }'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**cross-function — measured \\\\\\\"'`AFT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction f() { declare(ticks=2) { echo 'F'; } } declare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; } f();\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**repeat-function — measured \\\\\\\"'`F|FT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction f() { declare(ticks=2) { echo 'F'; } } f(); echo '|'; f();\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**cross-include — measured \\\\\\\"'`ALT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; } include 'lib.php';\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlib.php:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<?php declare(ticks=2) { echo 'L'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**unticked-include — measured \\\\\\\"'`ALTB`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; include 'lib.php'; echo 'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlib.php:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<?php echo 'L';\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**generator-shared — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABTC`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction g() { declare(ticks=2) { yield 1; } } \\\\\\\"'$a=g(); $b=g(); $a->current(); $b->current(); echo '\\\\\\\"'A'; \\\\\\\"'$a->next(); echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; \\\\\\\"'$b->next(); echo '\\\\\\\"'C';\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**registration-no-reset — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; } unregister_tick_function('tick_handler'); register_tick_function('tick_handler'); declare(ticks=2) { echo 'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**empty-registry — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nunregister_tick_function('tick_handler'); declare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; } register_tick_function('tick_handler'); declare(ticks=2) { echo 'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**semicolon-directive — measured \\\\\\\"'`ATB`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2); echo 'A'; echo 'B';\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**include-closure — measured \\\\\\\"'`AFBFT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ninclude 'lib.php'; echo 'A'; \\\\\\\"'$f(); echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; \\\\\\\"'$f();'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlib.php:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<?php \\\\\\\"'$f=function(){ declare(ticks=2) { echo '\\\\\\\"'F'; } };\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**exception-no-reset — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; } try { throw new Exception(); } catch (Exception \\\\\\\"'$e) {} declare(ticks=2) { echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**once-skip — measured \\\\\\\"'`LBT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ninclude_once 'lib.php'; include_once 'lib.php'; declare(ticks=2) { echo 'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlib.php:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<?php declare(ticks=2) { echo 'L'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Review scope and properties confirmed**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRead the repository architecture rules, slice-3 design, §12/§15, part-C brief/findings, staged programs/tests, PHP profile and shared after-wrapper, publication seam, and P7 oracle wrapper. Inspected the cited PHP-8.3 compiler/executor/generator/callback sources. Confirmed request-owned explicit state, lexical operand ownership, budget separation, after-normal-completion placement, and unchanged generic VM semantics as the intended architecture. Ran only the 21 direct PHP probes; no Clojure/Node/Dart implementation gates or formal corpus fold were run. The profile declaration exists, but \\\\\\\"'`php.sp/line`, lowering/registry integration, and linked site handoff remain the implementer'\\\\\\\"'s work.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\np = Path('/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p7b/collab/yang-php/1794567570000-architect-ticks-counter-ruling.gpt-6-astra.findings.md')\\\\nwith p.open('x') as f:\\\\n    f.write(content)\\\\nprint(str(p))\\\\nprint(str(len(content.splitlines())) + ' lines written')\\\\nP7B_WRITE_FINDINGS\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-php/1794567570000-architect-ticks-counter-ruling.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:54:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_27\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 - <<'P7B_WRITE_FINDINGS'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\ncontent = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-13 11:04:20 GMT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-13 18:04:20 +0700\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCoding-Agent: codex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRole: Architect, slice-3 design consult\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nReviewed checkout: p7b-ticks @ 38375bf7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nStatus: counter ruling complete; implementation and formal corpus acceptance remain outstanding\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Ruling: one counter per PHP request, with the threshold supplied by each selected statement-completion hook.** There is no counter per declare occurrence, source file, function/op_array, closure, or generator. Lexical scope controls which completion sites exist and their thresholds; it does not partition the runtime count.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis is supported both by PHP-8.3 source inspection and direct execution of 21 small programs on shiva's PHP 8.3.35 oracle image. All five staged expectations match. This consult changes only this findings artifact: no source, test, design-document, fixture-provenance, or branch changes; no commit or push.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Findings and reconciliation**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Severity | Location | Evidence / required correction |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| P1 — contradictory implementation instruction | \\\\\\\"'`collab/yang-php/1794567390000-engineer-p7b-ticks-c.prompt.md:20` | The explicit “a count is per declare-site, PHP semantics” instruction is incorrect. Replace it with the request-owned counter rule in this ruling. Part C was right to escalate the conflict instead of claiming parity. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Resolved — slice-3 ownership | \\\\\\\"'`collab/orch-lane/1794700000000-architect-safepoint-slice3-design.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:103` | The text explicitly says “request-owned counter” and says state survives calls, includes, and generator switches. Its lifecycle table at lines 123–127 and implementation assignment at line 257 reinforce that contract. The implementer'\\\\\\\"'s request-wide reading is correct. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| P2 — stale design status/timing | \\\\\\\"'`docs/design/yang.php.md:1938` | §12 still says sites are before statements and the generic extension refuses non-lambdas. The implemented after-wrapper is at `src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:153`; PHP'\\\\\\\"'s profile is at \\\\\\\"'`src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc:13`. Reconcile §12 in the implementation round. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| P1 — acceptance does not discriminate ownership | \\\\\\\"'`test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p7b.cljc:10` | Every staged tick threshold is 1. All these outputs can pass with an incorrectly partitioned counter. Add N>1 boundary/threshold cases below before claiming counter parity. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| P2 — oracle exit status is insufficient for pending rows | \\\\\\\"'`src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj:558` | Pending rows are excluded from failures, while `check-p7-fixture` at line 492 deliberately leaves their `:pass?` false. Read and compare actual records; exit 0 / “failures: 0” alone proves no parity for these rows. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI own the reconciliation failure between the design, stale documentation, and implementation brief. The slice-3 counter paragraph itself was explicit, not ambiguous. Its omission of a compact lexical-versus-runtime decision table made the broader artifact set easier to misread. At this checkout, neither §12 nor the §15 P7-b row (\\\\\\\"'`yang.php.md:2106`) actually specifies a per-declare counter; §15 requires PHP-equivalent tick counts. File-scoped compilation does not imply file-owned execution state.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**PHP 8.3 source evidence**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe links below refer to the PHP-8.3 branch inspected for this consult; line numbers are ordinary one-based file lines. They are source references, not a claim that the moving branch is the exact source hash of the oracle image.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Zend/zend_globals.h:187](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_globals.h#L187): \\\\\\\"'`ticks_count` is a field of executor globals.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Zend/zend_execute_API.c:151](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_execute_API.c#L151): \\\\\\\"'`init_executor()` initializes it to zero for execution/request startup.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Zend/zend_execute.c:5153](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_execute.c#L5153) includes generated \\\\\\\"'`zend_vm_execute.h`. The tick handler'\\\\\\\"'s maintained definition is [Zend/zend_vm_def.h:7439–7452](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_vm_def.h#L7439). Its test is \\\\\\\"'`(uint32_t)++EG(ticks_count) >= opline->extended_value`; it resets the count before calling the tick dispatcher. It counts even when no dispatcher is installed. This is an executor-global accumulator and an instruction-local threshold, not op_array-local state.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Compiler mechanism: [Zend/zend_compile.c:344–361](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L344) initializes a new file's compile-time ticks setting to zero and restores the prior file context on exit. [Lines 5938–5994](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L5938) convert the directive literal to a long, update that setting, compile a block, and restore its prior setting; the semicolon form leaves it changed. [Lines 7065–7200](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L7065) switch function op_arrays without starting a fresh file context. [Lines 9784–9785](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L9784) emit ticks after selected statements when the setting is nonzero. [Lines 2110–2121](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L2110) place that setting in the instruction's extended operand and suppress adjacent duplicate tick emission. [Lines 2518–2522](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L2518) enumerate excluded statement categories; [lines 9659–9668](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_compile.c#L9659) separately handle top-level function/class declarations. A blanket “hook every AST statement” translation is insufficient.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [Zend/zend_vm_def.h:7867–7874](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_vm_def.h#L7867): yield saves the next instruction and returns. [Zend/zend_generators.c:706–828](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/Zend/zend_generators.c#L706) restores execution frames/JIT context around resume, not a saved tick count.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- [ext/standard/basic_functions.c:1549–1569](https://github.com/php/php-src/blob/PHP-8.3/ext/standard/basic_functions.c#L1549): user tick dispatch guards each executing registered entry against reentry. Do not replace this with a global “ticks busy” rule that stops counting all guest tick sites. Registered callback arguments are its registration arguments, not the line/unit/threshold operands.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThus switching files or op_arrays changes the instructions being executed, and possibly their embedded thresholds, without selecting a different counter. The runtime probes below independently confirm the relevant observable consequences.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Normative decision table for the implementer**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Concern | Required behavior |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|---|---|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Counter owner | Allocate one explicit guest request-owned counter, initially 0, shared by all PHP tick hooks in that request. Keep it in existing guest execution/store machinery; introduce no host global or shared process state. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Increment and firing | On each selected normal completion, increment once. If the new count is **greater than or equal to** that site's N, reset to 0 **before** dispatching registered handlers. Do not use equality, modulo, subtraction of N, or a threshold-global “current N.” |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Reset points | Request initialization and threshold firing only. No reset at declare entry/exit, function call/return, include/return, registration/unregistration, generator switch, or exception/context restoration. A new independent request starts from zero. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Empty registry | Continue incrementing/resetting at selected sites. Registration changes dispatch membership, not counter phase. Confirmed by the empty-registry probe. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Lexical N | Each mark carries its own effective compile-time N. An inner block directive overrides the enclosing value for its body; exiting that block restores the outer value for subsequent emitted sites. Entering/leaving either block does not reset the accumulated count. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| N=0 | That lexical region contributes no tick instructions for its own statements; it does not clear accumulated progress. An enclosing nonzero context may still select the completion of the declare construct itself. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Directive syntax | Preserve block versus semicolon behavior and Zend's statement-selection/adjacent-suppression behavior. A directive can itself lead to a tick: the measured semicolon case below produces ATB, not ABT. There is no extra generic “enter declare” runtime reset or hook. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| N validation/range | Ordinary positive integer thresholds and zero are the cases established here. Do not invent “all N<=0 disable ticks”: Zend's literal conversion and unsigned instruction operand are separate concerns. Broader literal/range acceptance needs its own oracle cases or an explicit supported-subset refusal. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Functions and closures | Retain body-site thresholds from compilation. A call from ticked code does not dynamically instrument an unticked body. A ticked body contributes to the same request count even when called from unticked code or after its defining include has returned. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Generator yield/resume | Preserve the pending after-hook in the continuation. Suspension itself does not complete the yield statement. On eventual normal completion run that hook once using the then-current request counter. Repeated inspection of a suspended value does not replay it. Never snapshot/restore the count with generator context. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Nonlocal exit | A statement whose normal completion is bypassed contributes no after-hook. Already completed sites retain their count effects through throw/unwind. A callback exception cannot undo the reset that preceded dispatch. A pending hook is not a finally hook. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Include/include_once | Included code has its own lexical sites/N; the caller's pragma is not inherited dynamically. All executed sites share the request counter. Repeated includes revisit their sites; a skipped once body contributes none. A selected caller include statement still completes and can tick even when the once body is skipped. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Budget/profile separation | Statement ticks do not charge \\\\\\\"'`php.sp/tick`, the existing execution-budget hook. Preserve independently selected `:call`/`:loop` sites and the shared VM semantics. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe intended profile and operand contract remains exactly:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```clojure'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n{:line {:hook 'php.sp/line :operands true :after true}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n[:line n {:unit unit-path :ticks N}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n;; derives:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(php.sp/line n {:unit unit-path :ticks N})\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nHere \\\\\\\"'`n` and `:unit` identify the source occurrence; neither is a counter key. `:ticks` is the effective instruction threshold, not a declaration identifier. The generic safepoint stage transports literals and performs value-preserving normal-completion placement; PHP lowering owns eligible-site selection and PHP runtime code owns counting/dispatch. Omitting `:line` from a derivation profile omits these hooks; canonical program rows remain unchanged.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Include-site handoff remains a landing requirement**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source-unit operand does not itself transport marks through publication. At \\\\\\\"'`src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc:42`, `:site-set` is still nil. Preserve slice-3 lines 133–154: publish and retrieve verified occurrence site sets bound to the canonical root/source association; derive included executable images using the selected ticks profile; pin the hook dependency and derived images; handle SCC bundles and repin member aliases. Missing required metadata must fail closed, whereas a verified empty set for an unticked unit is legitimate.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEvery derived module must resolve the same request's hook/state. Including a module must not reinitialize the tick registry or accumulator. A retained closure keeps its defining unit's operands and uses the active request's shared counter. No extra counter indexed by declaration, unit, or line is needed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Measured fixture evidence**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nExecuted on \\\\\\\"'`shiva.stigmergy.systems`, 2026-11-13, in fresh disposable containers per program. Existing tag `php:8.3-cli` reports PHP 8.3.35 CLI NTS / Zend 4.3.35, built 2026-10-06. The shorter `php:8.3` tag was not installed; no image was pulled.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Image ID: \\\\\\\"'`sha256:7855de8f54c32ffc92720b20b550f2dbc1c82c2000c7a850ccf350f71c36293f`'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Repository digest: \\\\\\\"'`php@sha256:aafe21201943a8a6e497ddfb471e2ce68ada76adede38c7d61fede8918b24319`'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEach main program and included unit was placed in a temporary directory, mounted read-only at /w, with this invocation:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```sh'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndocker run --rm --pull=never --network=none --read-only \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -v <temporary-directory>:/w:ro -w /w php:8.3-cli php \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -d display_errors=1 -d html_errors=0 -d error_reporting=E_ALL \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -d log_errors=0 -d auto_prepend_file=/w/pre.php main.php\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe unticked pre.php was the exact staged prologue:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n<?php function tick_handler() { echo 'T'; } register_tick_function('tick_handler');\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis matches the P7 oracle runner's prepend-unit arrangement. Every one of the 21 executions exited 0 with empty stderr and exactly the stdout recorded here, with no diagnostics. Temporary directories were removed. These are independent direct PHP oracle measurements, **not** a run of the Clojure \\\\\\\"'`--p7` wrapper or of yang.php.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Fixture and source location | Staged expected | Measured PHP 8.3.35 | Interpretation |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n|---|---|---|---|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| sequence, \\\\\\\"'`programs_p7b.cljc:10` | ATTBT | ATTBT | Three completions: echo A, assignment, echo B. |'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| loop-body, line 12 | ATAT | ATAT | Only the inner declared body is ticked; loop machinery is outside its directive. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| function-call, line 14 | FT | FT | f's body is unticked; the call statement's normal completion ticks. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| generator-resume, line 16 | ATBT | ATBT | current() suspends at yield; A prints; next() completes yield and ticks, then B completes and ticks. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| include-handoff, line 19 | LT | LT | Included lib.php owns a ticked echo site; the caller is unticked. |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe sequence variants also confirm the slice-3 proposals: N=2 gives ATB; N=0 gives AB.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Oracle acceptance ruling**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThere is no remaining choice between counter architectures: the source mechanism and the N>1 measurements settle it in favor of the request-owned count. PHP remains the authority for exact site selection and observable output if a lowering prediction disagrees.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe formal \\\\\\\"'`--p7` pass on shiva MUST compare all five current IDs: `:sequence`, `:loop-body`, `:function-call`, `:generator-resume`, and `:include-handoff`, including output, absence of diagnostics/uncaught errors, and successful exit. Record actual version, image digest, host, and date. Do not infer a passing fixture from the current runner'\\\\\\\"'s pending-row exit status. This consult leaves all \\\\\\\"'`:oracle :pending` fields untouched.'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor counter-ownership acceptance, the implementer must add and oracle-confirm at least separate-declares, nested-threshold, cross-function, cross-include, and generator-shared from the appendix. Also retain the zero-gap, unticked-include, registration/empty-registry, retained-closure, exception, once-skip, and semicolon regressions. The original five N=1 rows cannot replace these discriminators. P7-b's remaining lowering/runtime/linking gates and the broader slice-3 callback/escape/cleanup cases remain required; this consult is not implementation sign-off.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**Reproducible additional probes**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nEach source below is main.php after an opening PHP tag, with the same separate pre.php above. Where shown, lib.php is a separate file. Outputs are observations, not new hand-derived goldens.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**sequence-n2 — measured \\\\\\\"'`ATB`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; \\\\\\\"'$x = 1; echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**sequence-n0 — measured \\\\\\\"'`AB`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=0) { echo 'A'; \\\\\\\"'$x = 1; echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**separate-declares — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=2) { echo 'A'; } declare(ticks=2) { echo 'B'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**nested-threshold — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABCTD`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=5) { echo 'A'; \\\\\\\"'$x=1; echo '\\\\\\\"'B'; declare(ticks=2) { echo 'C'; } echo 'D'; }\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**zero-gap — measured \\\\\\\"'`ABCT`.**'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndeclare(ticks=3) { echo 'A'; } declare(ticks=0) { echo 'B'; } declare(ticks=3) { 